      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Real‑Time GPS Tracking &amp; Transparent Communication During Bike Transport</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">The satellite GPS live‑tracking system forms the backbone of our bike‑parcel service, delivering centimeter‑level positioning data every few seconds from orbiting constellations to the cloud. Each parcel is equipped with a compact, low‑power GPS module that continuously receives signals from multiple satellites, fuses them with cellular or LoRaWAN fallback links, and pushes a timestamped latitude/longitude packet to our secure data hub. Because the device can lock onto at least four satellites at any moment, the location feed remains uninterrupted even in dense urban canyons or remote countryside, offering a reliability that rivals the **bike transport Indian railways** benchmark for punctuality and traceability.

Once the data reaches the hub, it is processed by a real‑time analytics engine that enriches the raw coordinates with geofencing, route‑optimisation, and estimated‑time‑of‑arrival (ETA) calculations. The results are instantly reflected in the customer portal, a web‑based dashboard accessible on desktop or mobile browsers. Users log in to see a live map with a moving icon that mirrors the parcel’s exact position, a timeline of status changes (picked up, in transit, customs cleared, out‑for‑delivery), and a dynamic ETA that updates as traffic or weather conditions evolve.

Portal alerts are fully customisable. Clients can subscribe to push notifications, SMS, or email triggers for events such as “parcel entered destination city,” “delay beyond 30 minutes,” or “delivery window approaching.” Alerts are throttled to avoid spamming, yet they guarantee that every stakeholder—logistics managers, retailers, or end‑customers—receives timely, actionable information.

Monitoring bike‑parcel status is therefore as simple as opening the portal, selecting the shipment ID, and watching the live trace. The interface also provides historical playback, allowing users to audit the exact route taken, compare it against service‑level agreements, and generate reports for compliance or insurance purposes. By leveraging satellite GPS precision and an intuitive alert system, our solution delivers the same dependable tracking experience that the **bike transport Indian railways** is known for, but with instant, digital visibility for every parcel on the road.</div>
