      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Comprehensive Insurance &amp; Documentation Checklist for Bike Shipping</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">**⚠️ ALERT – DOCUMENT CHECKLIST FOR HASSLE‑FREE REIMBURSEMENT CLAIMS**  
*Bike parcel shipped by train – IRDAI‑approved full‑value insurance, original RC, e‑Way bill & GST invoice*  

---

### 1️⃣ IRDAI‑Approved Full‑Value Insurance  

**Why it matters:** Reimbursement is payable only up to the insured amount. An IRDAI‑approved policy eliminates disputes over “partial” or “un‑approved” coverage, ensuring the insurer honors the full claim without delay.

---

### 2️⃣ Original Registration Certificate (RC) for the Bike  

**Why it matters:** Transport authorities and the railway’s cargo department require the RC to verify that the parcel is a registered motor vehicle. Missing or forged RCs lead to cargo hold, fines, or outright denial of reimbursement.

---

### 3️⃣ e‑Way Bill Compliance  

**Why it matters:** Under the GST Act, any movement of goods above ₹50,000 without a valid e‑Way Bill is a penalizable offense. Auditors reject reimbursement claims lacking a compliant e‑Way Bill, citing “illegal transport”.

---

### 4️⃣ GST‑Compliant Invoice  

**Why it matters:** GST input‑tax credit can be claimed only against a *properly issued* GST invoice. Finance teams reject any claim lacking this document, leading to delayed or denied reimbursement.

---

### QUICK REMINDER  

*Adhering to this checklist guarantees that every reimbursement claim proceeds smoothly, without unnecessary queries or penalties.*</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



